# Hermes gateway-mode c2c (research only)

**Research only.** No implementation, plugin, OCaml, or config in this idea.
No phases/tasks. Full evidence:
`.collab/research/2026-10-21T01-34-00Z-hermes-gateway-c2c-support.md`

## Goal

Record how (and whether) c2c can **wake** a Hermes agent that is running as a
**gateway** (Telegram / Discord / …), as distinct from spawning a **new**
API-server / webhook / A2A task. Preserve B098 (bus, never RPC), the peek →
inject → drain-on-success contract, and plugin-first Hermes (no `c2c start
hermes`).

## Current c2c plugin (this repo @ 56a34012)

- Plugin-first under `~/.hermes/plugins/c2c/`: tools, slash commands,
  `on_session_start` identity, `pre_llm_call` drain, daemon `BrokerWatcher`
  (stat 2s / safety 10s).
- Identity is **process-global**. Session id pinned before any `c2c` call
  (`hermes-*` only if inherited). Alias from whoami or `hermes-<hash>`.
  `on_session_start` fires on the **first turn**, not at launch — no alias
  until someone speaks.
- Wake = `ctx.inject_message` after peek. Drain only on True. Gateway today
  is **NONE, not lossy**.
- B098 envelope + U+2039 sanitization already in `delivery.py`.

## Upstream vs this machine

| Tree | SHA | `inject_message` |
|---|---|---|
| Local `~/.hermes/hermes-agent` | `0044876a` (2026-08-02) | CLI-only; gateway always False |
| GitHub `NousResearch/hermes-agent` main | `0b8dee00` (2026-10-21) | `session_key=` / `origin=` + `allow_gateway_injection` |

Design against **upstream**, version-gate the old 2-arg CLI-only signature.

## New API task vs wake existing Telegram

**Wake existing Telegram (what operators mean):** plugin
`inject_message(..., session_key=)` or `origin={platform, chat_id, …}` into a
chat that already has a committed human message. Internal event, queued if
busy, `allow_gateway_control=False`, skips pairing. Requires
`plugins.entries.c2c.allow_gateway_injection: true`.

**Not a Telegram wake:**

- API server `X-Hermes-Session-Id` of a messaging session → HTTP **409**
  `permission_denied` (API cannot bind a foreign surface).
- Webhook → new `webhook:{route}:{delivery_id}` session (one-shot).
- A2A → session keyed by `contextId` (`a2a:{peer}`), not `telegram:<chat>`.
- Gateway WS `prompt.submit` → local CLI/TUI sessions, needs operator creds
  (≈ forbidden `c2c start hermes`).
- Keyless `inject_message()` from `BrokerWatcher` (a **timer thread**) →
  refused unless exactly one attached classic CLI session exists.

So: **even after upgrading Hermes, today's watcher cannot wake Telegram**
without passing `session_key`/`origin`. That is the actual work.

## Identity / routing / lifecycle

Gateway = one process, N chats. Current plugin = one alias, one watcher, one
inbox. v1 should be a **home chat** (configured or first Telegram
`on_session_start`), one c2c alias. Per-chat aliases later. Cold start still
needs one human message in that chat (origin path cannot *open* a chat).

## Security (untrusted peers)

- Keep peek-drain; never drain-first (`--ephemeral` has no archive).
- Do not mint a Telegram session from peer mail.
- Plugin injects are internal DATA, not `/approve`/`/stop`.
- Add plugin-side ping-pong / rate cap (A2A uses `A2A_MAX_PINGPONG_TURNS=5`,
  `A2A_RATE_LIMIT=60/min`). Watcher at 2s can otherwise start a turn every
  tick.
- Busy = queue, never interrupt an in-flight operator turn.
- Webhook HMAC / A2A bearer / `API_SERVER_KEY` are for **out-of-process**
  callers; worse than in-process `allow_gateway_injection`.
- Relay peers remain untrusted DATA (existing skill / `docs/security/trust-model.md`).

## Avenues

| ID | Path | Telegram wake? | Use |
|---|---|---|---|
| **A** | Plugin `inject_message(session_key`/`origin)` + consent + home-chat | **Yes** (Hermes main) | **v1** |
| B/C | Raw `handle_message` / `deliver_wake` | Yes, internal | Don't bypass PluginContext |
| D | WS `prompt.submit` | Local only | No |
| E | API steal Telegram session id | **409** | Forbidden |
| F | API new session / `/v1/runs` | No | Optional later *different* peer |
| G/H | Webhook / `deliver_only` Telegram | Notify or new run | Backstop only |
| I | A2A as c2c transport | A2A session | Hermes↔Hermes without relay, not Telegram |
| J | `c2c monitor` | No Monitor on gateway | No |
| K | `pre_llm_call` drain | Activity only | Keep as complement |
| L | Upstream `gateway_start` hook | Arm at boot | Nice-to-have |
| M | Version-detect old vs new inject | Compat | **Required** |

## Recommendation

Implement **A + M** in a later claimed slice (not this idea): home-chat
targeted inject, opt-in `allow_gateway_injection`, peek-drain preserved,
ping-pong cap, refuse drain on False. Non-goals v1: API task peer, A2A
transport, webhook sidecar, `c2c start hermes`, per-chat aliases, interrupting
Telegram.

Do **not** advertise “enable API server and POST a completion” as gateway c2c
support.

